Third-party components
----------------------

None. Memory has no third-party dependency and no CDN.

Vendored from this project's own kits (same licence, same author), copied verbatim on
26/11/2026:

- web-kit 0.1.0 — docs/play/web-kit.js — the offline shell, storage helpers and PWA registration
- export-kit 1.0.0 — docs/play/export-kit.js — Blob download, used for the ciphertext export

Neither kit is modified. Neither makes a network request.

Cryptography
------------

AES-256-GCM with a 96-bit random IV per capture, and a key derived from the passphrase with
PBKDF2-SHA256 at 150,000 iterations over a 128-bit random salt. Both use the platform's WebCrypto
implementation — this app ships no cryptography of its own, which is the only responsible way to do
it. The salt is stored (it is not secret); the key and the passphrase are not.

What is stored in the clear: the time of each capture, a kind label, the clip length, and the
"no words heard" flag. Everything the person typed — the words and the place — is inside the
ciphertext.

What this app is not
--------------------

It is not a backup service and it cannot recover a forgotten passphrase. If the passphrase is lost,
the store is lost: that is the same property that makes it private.
